 Record design decisions, hypotheses, review findings, and unresolved questions here.
 Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+
+## 2026-10-24 minimum-padding teaching repair
+
+Version 2.2.0 repairs a frequent query-only shortcut: three demonstrations could
+all have motif boxes at least 3x3, allowing a no-minimum-padding rival to fit until
+a thin or single-cell query. Every three consecutive default samples now include
+a thin or single-cell motif, while explicit texture overrides remain exact.
+
+Generated motif colors now exclude the row-0 indicator color, constructively
+showing that the indicator—not a motif color—selects the frame. Three executable
+rivals are declared: no minimum padding, frame from the first motif cell, and
+frame from the modal motif color. The retained seed-0/easy/indices 4–7 case is
+protected-Racket labeled and all three rivals are refuted by the demonstrations.
+A bounded post-repair census checked 3,000 rolling windows (100 seeds × 10 starts ×
+three bands) with zero surviving declared rival. The result covers only those
+finite rivals and samples.
+
