+
+## 2026-10-24 mirror-branch teaching repair
+
+Version 3.1.0 repairs the retained query-only color-2 shortcut. Default samples
+now cycle constructively through `mirror_only`, `preserve_only`, and `both`, so
+any three consecutive examples contain evidence for both the special color-2
+horizontal reflection and ordinary orientation-preserving copies. Canonical-form
+sampling is retained within matching branch classes, and exact overrides remain
+unscheduled.
+
+Two executable rivals are declared: preserve every copy and mirror every copy.
+`lesson_identifiable` rejects a lesson when either rival survives the demos and
+changes the query. The historical seed 800009 / easy / indices 36–39 case is now
+protected-Racket labeled and both rivals are refuted by the first three examples.
+A bounded post-repair census checked 3,000 rolling windows (100 seeds × 10 starts ×
+three bands) with zero surviving declared rival. This is finite evidence, not a
+universal uniqueness proof.
+
+The inherited tests were also made portable by resolving canonical data through
+`reviewer_support`. The active canonical ledger and `GROUNDED_RULES` agree on rule
+hash `d31dc299f026`; the separate shared legacy base JSON remains stale and lies
+outside this assigned task home, so owner synchronization of that shared file is
+still pending.
+
